A||||4||Eric||Electrical Problem!!!||||8||
Z||000000||Eric||01-31-2000||03:57 PM||||For some reason my tach, voltmeter, parking brake light and who knows what else isn't working.  The car has been outside for a few days and snow may have gotten into some of the engine compartment.  It still runs.  I recently put in some aftermarket gauges including a voltmeter.  I may have got my wires crossed, but I really doubt it.  Would this make the tach not work also and continue not working even after the wiring problem was resolved?  I looked for a ten amp fuse that may have needed to be replaced, but I could find none.  I hope I can get everything operational again soon. Any ideas?  Thanks.||||reg||8
Z||000001||batboy||01-31-2000||08:05 PM||||Check the fuse labeled "gauges" in the fuse box. It should be in the outside row closest to the driver's door, about 3 fuses down. If the correct 10 amp fuse is in there it should be red in color. If that fuse is ok, check all the fuses one at a time. After that, you're on your own, sorry.||||reg||1
Z||000002||daved||01-31-2000||08:47 PM||||I think Batboy has it! You should find that coolant temp gauge, Tach, Fuel gauge and a bunch of dash warning lights etc. will not work with that fuse blown.  Disconnect your new equipment before you replace the fuse...I'm betting something you added has a short. <BR> To prove this, turn the key to the "bulb test" position (just before cranking) and your dash bulbs should light, and the temp. gauge wraps itself almost vertical!  When the fuse blows, none of the above happens, but the engine still runs normally.<BR>Let us know how you get on, D.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric||01-31-2000||10:37 PM||||After a closer inspection, I found the blown fuse.  It was a 15 amp fuse, that's why I didn't find it right away.  Thanks guys.||||reg||3
Z||000004||batboy||02-01-2000||12:00 AM||||Eric, careful dude! Something's goofy, maybe a short. You popped a 15 amp fuse that was supposed to be only a 10 amp one. That should be sending a warning signal to you.||||reg||1
